`packages/mkapp` is deleted. Two tools were doing one job. `dashboard-core`
plus `dashboard-ex` is a document with an Elixir seam and a collaborative
viewer being built on it, so a Svelte scaffolder over a single-writer JSON
store had no second reason to exist.

## What replaces it

`Dashboard.open("<id>")` in a kernel cell serves a document and returns its
browser URL. `Dashboard` is already in the workspace prelude, so a response
needs no scaffold, no `npm install`, no dev server, and no promote gate.
Sections are panes: `Dashboard.html/4` for prose and layout,
`Dashboard.data/5` for structured results. Republishing a pane id replaces
that pane in an already-open page, which is what a green promote used to do
and what the `generativeUiOutput` rule now tells agents to do instead.

One thing the dashboard has that mkapp did not: the reader can type into the
document. `Dashboard.view(doc)` wakes the session when they do and
`Dashboard.value(doc)` reads it back, so the question an agent wants answered
next can be answered in place rather than in chat.

## What went with it

Everything mkapp owned, in one change and with no shim: the CLI, the Svelte 5
template with its vendored shadcn-svelte registry and generated ghostty theme,
the `mkapp-scaffold` flake check, and the `tsconfig.VARIANT.json` filename
allowance that existed only for the template's `tsconfig.staging.json`.

One thing stays for now. `IxMcp.Serve`, the kernel's `Serve.app` and its
staging gate, is mkapp-shaped end to end and is not general: it runs
`npm run check:staging` and `npm run promote`, polls a `staging/` tree, and
preflights with an error naming `mkapp`. It goes in a follow-up rather than
here, because a live report page is still being served by its jobs and the
dashboard replacement is not finished. Deleting it today would open a window
with no working generative-UI surface at all. Until that follow-up its
moduledoc and its preflight error still name a command that no longer exists.

The version-history work in flight for mkapp (ENG-11106, index#4376) goes with
the package rather than landing first. Its `shape.ts` reconciler fixed a real
bug, a page blanking on `JSON.parse(raw) as AppState` after a shape change,
and that bug does not exist here: the document holds the state and no cast
stands between a promote and a render. The `node --test` step that PR added to
`check:staging` was scoped to the template's own `package.json`, not to any
repo-wide gate, so nothing general is lost with it.

## Two dated posts stay wrong on purpose

`mkapp-serve-gated-hot-reload` and `mkapp-shadcn-svelte` describe what was
true when they were written and are left alone. Rewriting a dated post to
remove something that existed makes it false.
